-- Q5 [Bone Structure & Marrow] hard skill2 ans=A
WITH q AS (
  INSERT INTO questions (section, topic, subtopic, question_text, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, foundation, content_category, discipline, cognitive_skill, estimated_time_seconds)
  VALUES ('bio_biochem', 'The Musculoskeletal System', 'Bone Structure & Marrow', 'A comparative anatomy lab labels specimens to teach students how skeletons are organized across animals. Considering how the vertebrate skeleton is partitioned and how it differs from the arthropod body covering, which of the following classifications is/are correct?

I. The scapula and clavicle of a human shoulder belong to the appendicular skeleton.
II. The human vertebral column and ribs belong to the appendicular skeleton.
III. The chitinous covering of a beetle is an internal endoskeleton.', '[{"label": "A", "text": "I only"}, {"label": "B", "text": "III only"}, {"label": "C", "text": "I and III only"}, {"label": "D", "text": "II and III only"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'This is a Biology question that falls under the content category ''Organ Systems.'' The answer is A because only statement I correctly assigns a structure to its skeletal division: the scapula and clavicle form the pectoral girdle, an appendicular structure that attaches the upper limb to the axial skeleton. The skeleton is subdivided into two major divisions, axial and appendicular; the appendicular skeleton includes all bones of the upper and lower limbs plus the bones that attach each limb to the axial skeleton, and the bones that attach the upper limb to the axial skeleton form the pectoral girdle, consisting of the scapula and clavicle. The axial skeleton, by contrast, forms the vertical central axis of the body and consists of the skull, the vertebral column, and the thoracic cage (the 12 pairs of ribs and the sternum). A vertebrate endoskeleton is an internal skeleton, whereas the arthropod exoskeleton is a hard external covering made of chitin. (Choice A) is correct: statement I alone is accurate, because the scapula and clavicle (the pectoral girdle) attach the upper limb to the axial skeleton and are therefore appendicular. (Choice B) is wrong because statement III misclassifies the beetle''s covering; the chitinous shell of an arthropod is an external exoskeleton, not an internal endoskeleton, so III is false and cannot be the sole correct statement. (Choice C) is wrong because it pairs the true statement I with the false statement III; the beetle''s chitinous exoskeleton is external, so III does not belong. (Choice D) is wrong because both statements it names are false: the vertebral column and ribs are part of the axial skeleton, not the appendicular skeleton, and the beetle''s chitin is an exoskeleton, not an endoskeleton. This is a Scientific Reasoning and Problem Solving question because you must apply the axial/appendicular and endoskeleton/exoskeleton classification rules to several named structures and determine which assignments hold.', 'hard', '3B', 'Organ Systems', 'biology', 2, 150)
  RETURNING id
)
