-- Q10 [Bone Matrix & Microstructure] medium skill2 ans=B
WITH q AS (
  INSERT INTO questions (section, topic, subtopic, question_text, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, foundation, content_category, discipline, cognitive_skill, estimated_time_seconds)
  VALUES ('bio_biochem', 'The Musculoskeletal System', 'Bone Matrix & Microstructure', 'A researcher soaks an intact long bone in a dilute acid bath that selectively dissolves the hydroxyapatite crystals while leaving the collagen fibers intact. Which of the following changes in the bone''s mechanical behavior is the treated bone most likely to show?

I. The bone shatters more easily when struck.
II. The bone becomes harder and more rigid.
III. The bone bends instead of supporting a load.', '[{"label": "A", "text": "I only"}, {"label": "B", "text": "III only"}, {"label": "C", "text": "I and III only"}, {"label": "D", "text": "II and III only"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'This is a Biology question that falls under the content category ''Organ Systems.'' The answer is B because dissolving the inorganic hydroxyapatite removes the hardness and rigidity of bone while leaving the flexible collagen behind, so the bone bends rather than supporting weight. Bone''s matrix has two components: the inorganic mineral, calcium phosphate and calcium carbonate crystallized as hydroxyapatite \(\text{Ca}_{10}(\text{PO}_4)_6(\text{OH})_2\), which gives bone hardness and strength, and the organic collagen fibers, which give bone flexibility so it is not brittle. The textbook states the consequence of removing each component directly: \"Without collagen, bones would be brittle and shatter easily. Without mineral crystals, bones would flex and provide little support.\" Because acid removes only the mineral crystals here, the remaining collagen-rich bone flexes and can no longer bear a load, matching statement III. (Choice A) I only is wrong because shattering and brittleness result from losing collagen, not mineral; with collagen preserved, the bone resists shattering. (Choice B) is correct: with the mineral dissolved, only the flexible organic collagen remains, so the bone flexes and provides little support, exactly as statement III describes. (Choice C) I and III only is wrong because statement I describes the opposite manipulation, loss of collagen, which is not what the acid does here, so only statement III applies to mineral removal. (Choice D) II and III only is wrong because statement II reverses the relationship; removing the hydroxyapatite that supplies hardness makes the bone softer and more pliable, not harder and more rigid. This is a Scientific Reasoning and Problem Solving question because you must apply the distinct contributions of the organic and inorganic matrix to predict the mechanical outcome of removing one component.', 'medium', '3B', 'Organ Systems', 'biology', 2, 110)
  RETURNING id
)
