-- Q22 [Joints & Movement] medium skill2 ans=B
WITH q AS (
  INSERT INTO questions (section, topic, subtopic, question_text, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, foundation, content_category, discipline, cognitive_skill, estimated_time_seconds)
  VALUES ('bio_biochem', 'The Musculoskeletal System', 'Joints & Movement', 'An anatomist examines three fibrous connective-tissue bands at the human knee and ankle and traces the structures that each band connects:

I. A band joining the gastrocnemius muscle to the calcaneus
II. A band that transmits the pull of the quadriceps femoris to the tibial tuberosity
III. A band uniting the anterior surfaces of two adjacent vertebral bodies

Which of these bands most likely function as ligaments that stabilize a joint by anchoring bone to bone?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "I only"}, {"label": "B", "text": "III only"}, {"label": "C", "text": "I and III only"}, {"label": "D", "text": "II and III only"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'This is a Biology question that falls under the content category ''Organ Systems.'' The answer is B because only band III connects one bone to another bone, which is the defining role of a ligament in stabilizing a joint. A ligament is a strong band of fibrous connective tissue that holds the bones at a moveable joint together and prevents excessive or abnormal joint movements, anchoring the bones and preventing their separation. By contrast, a tendon is the dense connective tissue structure that attaches a muscle to bone, so that when the muscle contracts it pulls on the bone to transmit force and produce movement. Band III, uniting the anterior surfaces of adjacent vertebral bodies (a bone-to-bone connection, as the anterior longitudinal ligament does), is therefore a ligament, whereas bands I and II each link a muscle to a bone and are tendons. (Choice A) I only is incorrect because band I joins a muscle (gastrocnemius) to a bone (calcaneus); a muscle-to-bone band is a tendon that transmits contractile force, not a bone-to-bone ligament. (Choice B) is correct: band III is the only band that connects bone to bone (adjacent vertebral bodies), the role of a ligament, which strengthens and supports the joint by anchoring the bones together and resisting their separation. (Choice C) I and III only is incorrect because it wrongly includes band I; band I attaches muscle to bone and is a tendon, so only III qualifies as a ligament. (Choice D) II and III only is incorrect because band II attaches the quadriceps muscle to the tibia and is a tendon transmitting muscle force, not a bone-to-bone stabilizer; only III is a ligament. This is a Scientific Reasoning and Problem Solving question because you must apply the bone-to-bone versus muscle-to-bone attachment criteria to classify several described connective-tissue bands as ligaments or tendons.', 'medium', '3B', 'Organ Systems', 'biology', 2, 105)
  RETURNING id
)
